00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:05.910 align:start position:0%
 
i had  five messages for the leaders today  the first one is on data sharing  we have to share comprehensive and  accurate  data in real time with the ecdc platform  we are making 220 million euros  available  to finance a safe cross-border transfer  of patients  where it is needed and for that the good  use of the money requires good  information in exchange  the second topic was also a topic on  sharing  but in this time in this case experience  and  analysis the third topic is testing  our goal is keeping the virus in check  and that goes through massive testing  the fourth topic is tracing  so testing and tracing go hand in hand  22 member states have developed  a tracing app or are developing a  tracing app  at the moment being we have  approximately 50 million  downloads concerning smart phone holders  but this is not enough therefore i asked  leaders in each country to encourage  a massive uptake by citizens so a  massive  download of the app by smartphone  holders  and finally the fifth point indeed is  vaccines and vaccination  we have three priorities here  the first is ensuring validation  of vaccines speedily and we do  have to do the validation at a good pace  while providing all the safety  guarantees  the second priority is to ensure indeed  the fair distribution of vaccines  to member states but thirdly before that  before  we really go into the vaccination indeed  the infrastructure for vaccination must  be ready  now is the time for patients for  determination and for discipline from  all of us  and that way altogether we will overcome  the virus  thank you

